# Audiotoolbox - TODO



## Performance

### `__array_finalize__` Overhead
- [ ] `SignalStats`, `Visualization`, and `TimeFrequency` are reconstructed on every slice/view.
      Make them lazy properties that only instantiate on first access:
      ```python
      @property
      def viz(self):
          if not hasattr(self, '_viz') or self._viz.sig is not self:
              self._viz = Visualization(self)
          return self._viz
      ```
      Apply same pattern to `stats` and `time_frequency`

### `FilterBank.filt` Loops
- [ ] `ButterworthBank.filt`: One `sosfilt` call per filter — `scipy.signal.sosfilt` accepts a
      batch axis. Replace the per-filter loop with a batched call
- [ ] `GammaToneBank.filt`: Same issue — loop over filters where batching is possible

### `convolve`
- [ ] Current implementation is an O(n²) Python loop over channel pairs.
      Replace with vectorised `fftconvolve` using broadcasting for the common cases.
      Consider splitting into `_convolve_matched` and `_convolve_outer` private methods
      to make each case independently readable and testable

### `to_analytical`
- [ ] Currently does two FFT round-trips (forward FFT → zero negative freqs → IFFT).
      Can be done in one pass — zero negative frequencies directly in the frequency domain
      without a separate `to_timedomain` call

### `copy_empty`
- [ ] `copy_empty` copies all data then zeroes it. Replace with:
      ```python
      def copy_empty(self):
          return np.zeros_like(self)
      ```

---

## Code Quality

### `BaseSignal`
- [ ] `_chIndexer` is reconstructed on every `.ch` access — cache it:
      ```python
      @property
      def ch(self):
          if not hasattr(self, '_ch_indexer'):
              self._ch_indexer = _chIndexer(self)
          return self._ch_indexer
      ```
- [ ] `Signal.__array_finalize__` returns `obj` — should return `None`
- [ ] `time_offset` defaults to `None` via `getattr(obj, "time_offset", None)` which
      causes `TypeError` in `time` property. Change default to `0`
- [ ] `plot()` raises `DeprecationWarning` instead of warning — use `warnings.warn(...)`

### `FrequencyDomainSignal`
- [ ] `to_analytical` modifies in-place but `to_timedomain` returns a new object —
      inconsistent API contract. Consider naming convention: `make_analytical()` vs `as_timedomain()`
- [ ] `angle = phase` class-level alias is fragile — replace with explicit `@property`
- [ ] `to_timedomain` copies `self` only to multiply by `n_samples` — pass scale directly:
      `wv = np.fft.ifft(self * self.n_samples, axis=0)`

### `FilterBank`
- [ ] Replace bare `Exception` with `ValueError` throughout
- [ ] Fix typo: `coefficents` → `coefficients` throughout (`ButterworthBank`, `GammaToneBank`)
- [ ] `_update_params`: Use `np.atleast_1d` to handle 0-d array edge case
- [ ] `__getitem__` with integer index collapses filter axis — wrap with `np.atleast_1d`:
      ```python
      bank.fc = np.atleast_1d(self.fc[i])
      bank.bw = np.atleast_1d(self.bw[i])
      bank.coefficients = self.coefficients[..., np.atleast_1d(i)]
      ```
- [ ] Add abstract `filt` method to `FilterBank` base class using `abc.ABC`
- [ ] `ButterworthBank.filt`: `.T` transpose fragile for N-D channels —
      replace `out_sig.T[i_filt] = out.T` with `out_sig.ch[..., i_filt] = out`
- [ ] Same `.T` issue in `BrickBank.filt`
- [ ] `GammaToneBank.__init__`: Calls `_update_params(**kwargs)` twice — remove redundant call
- [ ] `GammaToneBank` coefficient layout `[b0, unused, a0, a1]` — document the layout explicitly
- [ ] Squeeze behaviour in `GammaToneBank.filt` is inconsistent with other subclasses —
      move to parent or remove entirely
- [ ] `create_filterbank` return type annotation `Union[FilterBank, GammaToneBank, ...]`
      should simplify to `-> FilterBank`

### `ModificationMixin`
- [ ] `set_dbfs`, `set_dbspl`, `set_dbpeak` normalise per-channel independently,
      which changes relative levels between channels. Add `per_channel: bool = False` parameter
      or at minimum document the behaviour explicitly
- [ ] `delay` with `method='sample'` silently rounds sub-sample delays — add a warning
- [ ] `delay` has no `else` branch for invalid method — add `raise ValueError`
- [ ] `add_cos_modulator` docstring LaTeX has `f_m * t * φ₀` (multiply) but implementation
      correctly uses `+`. Fix docstring

### `Visualization`
- [ ] Replace `assert` with `raise ValueError` in `plot` and `specgram_overview`
- [ ] Replace `if not ax:` with `if ax is None:` in `plot` and `spectrum`
- [ ] `spectrum`: Remove dead variables `min_f = 20` and `max_f = 20000`
- [ ] `spectrum`: Single-sided amplitude correction (`*= 2`) is applied before dB conversion
      which is correct, but add a comment making the order dependency explicit

### `SignalStats`
- [ ] `dbc` docstring says "A weighted" — should say "C weighted"
- [ ] `dbfs` convention (0 dBFS = RMS of full-scale sine) should be documented explicitly —
      the other common convention (0 dBFS = peak = 1) differs by 3 dB
- [ ] `FreqDomainStats` inherits `mean`, `var`, `rms` from `BaseStats` but these are not
      meaningful for complex frequency domain bins — either override to raise `NotImplementedError`
      or add frequency-domain relevant properties (spectral centroid, total power via Parseval)

### `inst_cmplx_corr`
- [ ] Window is not normalised — divide by `win.sum()` for correct absolute magnitude.
      Phase is currently unaffected but magnitude will be wrong if `filt_iccp` is used directly
- [ ] Add coherence magnitude check — when `|coh|` is near 0, `phi_avg` is unreliable.
      Consider returning both phase and magnitude or exposing a `min_coherence` threshold

---

## Missing Tests

### Known Bugs Without Regression Tests
- [x] `zeropad(number=1, duration=1e-3)` — both args provided, should raise `ValueError`
- [x] `resample(-1000)` — negative int, should raise `ValueError`
- [x] `resample(24000.0)` — float input, should raise `ValueError`
- [x] `create_filterbank([100], [10], "unknown_type", 48000)` — raises `ValueError` (source fixed + test added)
- [x] `bank[0].filt(sig)` — scalar index then filt (source fixed via `atleast_1d` in `__getitem__` + test added)

### Missing Invariant Tests
- [x] FFT round-trip: `sig.to_freqdomain().to_timedomain() ≈ sig`
- [x] `set_dbfs` round-trip: `sig.set_dbfs(-20); assert sig.stats.dbfs ≈ -20`
- [x] `set_dbfs` inter-channel: documents per-channel normalization behavior (ratio changes independently)
- [x] `|inst_cmplx_corr| ≤ 1` for all inputs
- [x] Resample round-trip: `sig.resample(96000).resample(48000) ≈ original`

### Missing Filterbank Tests
- [x] Output shape consistency across all three filter types for identical inputs
- [x] Scalar `__getitem__` followed by `filt` for all subclasses
- [x] `ButterworthBank` with N-dimensional channel input

### Test Hygiene
- [x] Remove module-level executable code from `test_filterbank.py` —
      it runs on import during test collection and will cause confusing failures
- [x] Parametrize filter type tests using `@pytest.mark.parametrize`
- [x] Add pytest fixtures for common signals to reduce boilerplate
- [x] Fix loop variable shadowing in `test_butterworth` and `test_gammatone`:
      `for i_filt, (fc, bw)` shadows the outer `fc` and `bw` lists

